<title>USA: McGraw-Hill forms new unit.</title>
<headline>McGraw-Hill forms new unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>McGraw-Hill Cos said Tuesday it has created the Higher Education and Consumer Group, which includes the company's College Division, the pending acquisition of the Times Mirror Co's Higher Education Group, McGraw-Hill Home Interactive and future consumer initiatives.</p>
<p>It is anticipated that the acquisition will be completed in the fall subject to receipt of required government approval, the company noted.</p>
<p>It said Robert E. Evanson, 60, has been appointed president of the new group. He reports to Peter Jovanovich, president of McGraw-Hill's Educational and Professional Publishing Group.  Evanson previously served as executive vice president, Corporate Development.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
